%N A337501 Minimum number of painted cells in an n X n grid to avoid unpainted trominoes.
%H A337501 B. Brešar, M. Jakovac, J. Katrenič, G. Semanišin and A. Taranenko, <a href="https://omr.fnm.um.si/wp-content/uploads/2017/06/psn-v-revised01.pdf">On the vertex k-path cover</a>, preprint; <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dam.2013.02.024">journal version</a>, Discrete Applied Mathematics, 161 (2013), 1943-1949.
%F A337501 a(n) = n^2/2 if n is even, and n*(n-1)/2 + floor(n/3) if n is odd. - _Rahid Zaman_, Aug 30 2026
%e A337501 For n = 3, painting only 3 cells would leave an unpainted tromino, but painting the following 4 cells avoids all unpainted trominoes:
